LeetCode 26 – Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array

class Solution:
    def removeDuplicates(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        j=0
        for i in range(1,len(nums)):
            if nums[i]!=nums[j]:
                j+=1
                nums[j]=nums[i]
        return j+1
       
        
💡 Logic to Remember
The array is already sorted, so duplicates are adjacent.
Use two pointers:
i → points to the last unique element (slow pointer).
j → scans the array (fast pointer).

When nums[j] != nums[i]:

i += 1
nums[i] = nums[j]

Return:

i + 1

because i is an index, not the count.

🧠 Memory Trick

"Scan with j, write with i."

j finds the next unique element.
i stores it in the correct position.
i + 1 = number of unique elements.
